note bottom of TechnicianRanking
 Strategy (report §3.2, DEC-93).
 WorkloadRanking: last week's Active Hours, projected Active Hours,
 staff ID; classifyTechnicians() puts projected Credited >=40 h last (FR-55).
 ActivationRanking: eligible candidates only; fewest activated dates (12 months),
 then zone distance, then staff ID (FR-56).
end note

note bottom of Standby
 hours(): max(4, Staff.activeHoursOn(date)); once per date (DEC-96).
 Full-day Leave without duties has no minimum credit.
 activate(): idempotent; keep record and count this date once.
 effectiveZone(): Technician.homeZone for every source (DEC-97).
end note

legend bottom
One Crew per Van number per date; Crews per date <= VanAvailability.vansAvailable (FR-26, FR-32).
One StandbyPreference per Technician per week, and per day and Brand (FR-51).
At most one initial Crew/Standby placement. Activated Standby history remains with duties (FR-32).
Assignment: Crew present => 1 Driver + 1-2 Technicians; no Crew => exactly 1 certified Technician.
Assigned Staff are per-Job snapshots; Replacement changes only unstarted Jobs, preserving earlier Staff.
Crew.membersFor(job) applies replacements by effectiveFrom; fromJobId survives later unassignment.
Confirmed preferences cannot be overridden; capacity checked after locked inputs/CSVs (DEC-98).
Leave Records are read-only (FR-52).
Every control class that changes data calls AuditLog.record() (FR-49); RetentionJob purges rows older than 12 months (FR-58).
Drivers: assumed always enough; outside ranking and Standby (A1, DEC-82).
endlegend
